-### Hybrid Representation
-Hybrid Representation is a framework combining explicit feature storage and an implicit decoder to efficiently reconstruct and render radiance fields, addressing the computational expense of pure implicit NeRF [S8]. The steps are: 1. Store explicit features $V$ (e.g., voxel grid, hash table, basis vectors). 2. For any point $p$, efficiently obtain feature vector $v_p = V(p)$ (e.g., tri-linear interpolation). 3. Use a decoder $D$ (MLP or spherical harmonics) to map $v_p$ to density $\sigma$ and color $c$ [S8]. The Explicit Feature Storage $V$ can be a voxel grid, hash table, or set of basis vectors/matrices [S8]. The Decoder $D$ can be an MLP or spherical harmonics [S8].
